你穿的是同一件礼服吗？

315
00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:46.650
I didn't.
没有。

316
00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:47.910
I wore a different dress.
我穿了另一件。

317
00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:48.470
I don't know.
我不知道。

318
00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:50.550
I don't have any journal entry about this dress.
关于这件礼服我没有任何日记记录。

319
00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:51.970
It's just a little black dress.
就是一件黑色小礼服。

320
00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:57.410
And you know how at the Webby's, you can only say five words for your acceptance speech?
你知道威比奖的获奖感言只能说五个词吗？

321
00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:57.990
Yes.
知道。

322
00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:01.690
You remember this because we won a Webby in 2022.
你记得这个，因为我们在2022年赢过一个威比奖。

323
00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:07.030
The Office Ladies is a Webby's People's Voice winner in podcasts, television, and film.
《办公室女士》是威比奖播客、电视和电影类别的“人民之声”奖得主。

324
00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:09.850
Do you remember what our acceptance speech was?
你还记得我们的获奖感言是什么吗？

325
00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:15.050
I believe it ended with, that's what she said.
我记得结尾是“那是她说的”。

326
00:15:15.610 --> 00:15:18.950
Yes, it did, and I found it.
没错，确实是，我找到了。

327
00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:20.250
But what was the first word?
但第一个词是什么？

328
00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:21.010
Here we are.
我们在这儿。

329
00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:22.590
Speechless.
无言以对。

330
00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:23.930
That's what she said.
那是她说的。

331
00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:25.770
There it is.
就是这个。

332
00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.530
Well, I was curious.
嗯，我当时很好奇。

333
00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:30.010
I was like, what did I say?
我在想，我到底说了什么？

334
00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.130
What were my five words?
我的五个词是什么？

335
00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:31.890
I couldn't remember.
我记不起来了。

336
00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:36.810
And I knew it was like something about accounting, and I reached out to Joya, and she said, Angela,
我知道内容大概和会计有关，于是我联系了乔亚，她说，安吉拉，

337
00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:37.350
I remember.
我记得。

338
00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:38.190
I have it here.
我这儿有记录。

339
00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:39.210
And she sent it to me.
她发给我了。

340
00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:43.750
Our acceptance speech was, accounting is such a riot.
我们的获奖感言是：会计真是太搞笑了。

341
00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:48.850
And I said it just like that with my snarky Angela Martin face.
而且我当时就是用那副安吉拉·马丁式的刻薄表情说出来的。

342
00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:50.110
Amazing.
太棒了。

343
00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:51.970
So there you go.
所以就是这样。

344
00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:57.770
Well, something I think we should share is that you all filmed these for free.
嗯，我觉得我们应该分享一件事，那就是你们所有人都是免费拍摄这些内容的。

345
00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.690
Mike and Paul wrote these for free.
迈克和保罗也是免费写的剧本。

346
00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:09.650
And yes, you won two awards, but you have never received any compensation for these webisodes.
没错，你们赢得了两个奖项，但你们从来没有因为这些网络剧集获得过任何报酬。

347
00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:13.770
And NBC continues to monetize them on YouTube and Peacock.
而NBC还在YouTube和Peacock上利用它们获利。

348
00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:16.250
You do not receive residuals on them.
你们没有从中获得任何后续分成。

349
00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:20.230
And that is because this was what we were saying before.
这就是我们之前所说的原因。

350
00:16:20.470 --> 00:16:22.290
This was all new territory.
这在当时完全是全新的领域。

351
00:16:22.570 --> 00:16:26.990
It was originally seen as marketing and publicity for the show.
最初这被视为该节目的营销和宣传手段。

352
00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:27.630
Yeah.
没错。

353
00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:34.270
But after their success, you know, our unions, SAG and WGA,
但在它们成功之后，你知道，我们的工会，演员工会（SAG）和编剧工会（WGA），

354
00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:42.450
started to rethink how actors should be compensated for creating original content outside of the normal network broadcaSt.
开始重新思考演员在创作常规电视广播以外的原创内容时应如何获得报酬。

355
00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:56.950
I mean, the success of the webisodes really brought into focus all the ways that talent could become exploited if we didn't get some guardrails on this new medium.
我的意思是，网络剧集的成功确实让我们意识到，如果我们不为这种新媒介设立一些保障措施，演艺人才可能会以各种方式被剥削。

356
00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:57.870
That's right.
说得对。

357
00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:58.510
That's right.
说得对。

358
00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:02.050
I think that's kind of a cool thing that our show did.
我觉得我们节目做了一件挺酷的事。

359
00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:03.410
Yeah, I do too.
我也是这么觉得。

360
00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:12.750
And, you know, and we know people think that we sit around collecting like millions of dollars a year on residuals from the office.
而且，你知道，我们知道人们以为我们整天坐着就能从《办公室》的重播费里赚几百万美元。

361
00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:14.590
And we don't.
但我们并没有。

362
00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:20.030
We do not receive residuals on Peacock or Netflix or any of the streamers.
我们从 Peacock、Netflix 或任何流媒体平台那里都拿不到重播费。

363
00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:21.090
We never have.
从来都没有过。

364
00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:24.970
And that is because all of our contracts predated streaming.
那是因为我们所有的合同都签署于流媒体出现之前。

365
00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.990
It literally did not exiSt.
当时它根本就不存在。

366
00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:32.910
There was no language in our unions or in our contracts for how we would be compensated for it.
我们的工会条款或合同里没有任何关于我们该如何获得相关报酬的规定。

367
00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:36.830
Digital content was so new when we started the show.
我们刚开始做节目时，数字内容还非常新颖。

368
00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.830
I mean, clearly it was brand new.
我是说，显然那是全新的事物。

369
00:17:39.190 --> 00:17:39.490
Yes.
是的。

370
00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:46.190
Anyway, I would like to thank the webisodes for kicking off that conversation for Artists Everywhere.
总之，我要感谢这些网络剧集，是它们开启了关于广大艺术家权益的讨论。

371
00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:48.210
Oh, I love that.
噢，我喜欢这个说法。

372
00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:56.230
Well, Jenna, just to wrap this up really quickly before we get into the breakdown, if you'll notice, I just brought in my Emmy.
好了，Jenna，在进入剧情解析之前，简单总结一下，如果你注意到了，我刚才把我的艾美奖奖杯拿来了。

373
00:17:56.490 --> 00:17:57.690
I didn't bring in the Webby.
我没带威比奖（Webby）来。

374
00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:58.250
Yeah.
嗯。

375
00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:01.010
Because the Webby, I think, went to NBC Digital.
因为我觉得威比奖是颁给 NBC 数字部门的。

376
00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.250
Like, I didn't leave New York with a Webby.
我离开纽约时并没有带走威比奖。

377
00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:03.750
Okay.
好吧。

378
00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:10.470
But when we won this Daytime Emmy, they handed us this one Emmy to hold as we did our –
但当我们赢得这个日间艾美奖时，他们递给我们这一座奖杯让我们拿着拍照，就像我们做的那样——

379
00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:11.410
The photo op Emmy.
拍照用的艾美奖。

380
00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:12.350
The photo op Emmy.
拍照用的艾美奖。

381
00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:14.950
And I just said, I'm going to take it home.
然后我就说，我要把它带回家。

382
00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:16.270
And they were like, what?
他们当时就问，什么？

383
00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:19.310
And I was like, yeah, I'm going to take it home, and then you should send Brian an Oscar one, too.
我就说，对啊，我要把它带回家，而且你们也该给 Brian 和 Oscar 寄一个。

384
00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:26.450
And there was this look – there was this moment where they were like, that's not really your – and I was like, thank you.
当时出现了一种眼神——那一刻他们好像在说，那其实不是你的——但我说，谢谢啦。

385
00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:26.830
Bye.
再见。

386
00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:29.170
Lady, I love that.
天哪，我太喜欢这个了。

387
00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:30.930
I love that you did that.
我喜欢你这么做。

388
00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:34.230
You were like, I am not going to walk up on an Emmy stage again.
你当时就像是说，我可不会再走上艾美奖的舞台了。

389
00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.810
Because we didn't get one when we won the show.
因为我们节目获奖时，我们并没有拿到奖杯。

390
00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.510
No, none of the performers got it.
没有，演员们一个都没拿到。

391
00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:39.490
It went to the producers.
奖杯是给制片人的。

392
00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:40.270
Yeah.
没错。

393
00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:41.990
So I went home with the trophy.
所以我把奖杯带回了家。

394
00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:43.850
It had no writing on it.
上面什么字都没刻。

395
00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:48.050
And a few weeks later, in the mail, I got the plaque that went around it.
几周后，我收到了邮寄来的刻字铭牌，是贴在奖杯底座上的那种。

396
00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:51.330
I don't think I was meant to get this to take home.
我觉得这奖杯本不是让我带回家的。

397
00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:54.050
I think it's supposed to be on a shelf somewhere at NBC.
我觉得它应该放在 NBC 的某个架子上。

398
00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:55.610
Well, it's not.
嗯，它现在不在那儿。

399
00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:57.790
It's on our podcasting table right now.
它现在就在我们的播客桌上。

400
00:18:57.870 --> 00:18:59.690
And Brian and Oscar got one, too.
而且 Brian 和 Oscar 也各拿到了一个。

401
00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:00.450
Well done.
干得好。

402
00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:02.650
Well, those are our fast facts.
好了，以上就是我们的快速事实。

403
00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:03.550
Why don't we take a break?
我们休息一下好吗？

404
00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:08.870
And we will get into our breakdown with episode number one, The Books Don't Balance.
接下来我们将深入解析第一集，《账目不平》。

405
00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:09.430
Ooh.
噢。

406
00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:10.650
They all have titles.
它们都有标题。

407
00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:11.450
I love them all.
我全都喜欢。

408
00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:11.710
I know.
我知道。

409
00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:12.150
Me, too.
我也是。

410
00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:24.950
Here we go.
开始了。

411
00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:27.790
Episode one, The Books Don't Balance.
第一集，《账目不平》。

412
00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:33.210
We open on Jan, Oscar, Angela, and Brian in the conference room.
开场是简、奥斯卡、安吉拉和布莱恩在会议室里。

413
00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:33.730
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

414
00:19:34.430 --> 00:19:39.910
Angela delivers the news that they've discovered about $3,000 missing.
安吉拉宣布了他们发现有大约3000美元不见了的消息。

415
00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:43.310
Jan suggests this might be an accounting error.
简认为这可能是一个会计错误。

416
00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.690
And Angela's like, it is not an accounting error.
安吉拉却说，这绝不是会计错误。

417
00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:49.290
It's not her accounting error, at leaSt.
至少不是她的会计错误。

418
00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.130
Yeah, don't bring that BS my way, Jan.
没错，别把那套废话往我这儿推，简。

419
00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:54.530
She gives a little glare to Kevin.
她狠狠地瞪了凯文一眼。

420
00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:59.330
And we cut to his talking head, where he says, this is the first time hearing about it.
镜头切到凯文的采访，他说这是他第一次听说这件事。

421
00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:01.090
He's not heard of the accounting error.
他没听说过什么会计错误。

422
00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:02.750
He says nobody ever tells him anything.
他说从来没人告诉他任何事。

423
00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:03.850
And he likes it that way.
而且他乐得如此。

424
00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.430
He likes it that way.
他喜欢那样。

425
00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:08.650
Although later, we find out he's so excited to be a part of this.
尽管后来我们发现，他其实非常兴奋能参与其中。

426
00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:12.770
And angry that he's never allowed to write memos.
而且因为从不被允许写备忘录而感到愤怒。

427
00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:13.330
Exactly.
没错。

428
00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:17.550
Jan says they need to find the missing money, ASAP.
简说他们需要尽快找到那笔丢失的钱。

429
00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:21.030
You know, they want to ensure there's been no criminal activity.
你知道的，他们想确保没有发生任何犯罪活动。

430
00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:23.590
I have an improv moment for you.
我有一个即兴表演的片段要分享。

431
00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.090
I bet I know what it is.
我敢打赌我知道是什么。

432
00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:28.770
When Angela says, Michael said to stop by on your way out.
是安吉拉说“迈克尔让你走的时候顺便过去一下”那段吗？

433
00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:30.310
I knew it.
我就知道。

434
00:20:30.590 --> 00:20:31.170
You did.
你猜对了。

435
00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:35.130
You know my sort of improv voice now so well.
你现在已经非常了解我的即兴表演风格了。

436
00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:38.790
Again, I strategically put it at the very end, hoping it would make it.
再说一次，我特意把它放在最后，希望能被剪进正片里。

437
00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:41.410
Well, Angela, you just made someone very happy.
好吧，安吉拉，你刚刚让某人非常开心。

438
00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:43.450
We got a fan letter from Maria F.
我们收到了一封来自巴西的玛丽亚·F的粉丝来信，

439
00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.090
in Brazil who wanted to know if there were any jokes
她想知道是否有任何笑话

440
00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:50.450
or scenes that were improvised or if it was all scripted.
或场景是即兴发挥的，还是全部都有剧本。

441
00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:52.890
And Maria also said, I really love The Office.
玛丽亚还说，我真的很喜欢《办公室》。

442
00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:54.710
Angela is my favorite character.
安吉拉是我最喜欢的角色。

443
00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:55.670
Oh, Maria.
噢，玛丽亚。

444
00:20:55.930 --> 00:20:56.610
Thank you.
谢谢你。

445
00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.130
Big hugs to Brazil.
给巴西一个大大的拥抱。

446
00:20:58.550 --> 00:20:59.530
I'm loving it.
我太喜欢了。

447
00:20:59.890 --> 00:21:00.970
Well, Maria, here's the thing.
好吧，玛丽亚，情况是这样的。

448
00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.650
These were written really well, but we did have little moments.
剧本写得非常好，但我们确实有一些即兴的小瞬间。

449
00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.370
And I'll share those with you as we go.
我会随着节目的进行与你分享这些瞬间。

450
00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:11.770
Mine, Melora as Jan's reaction was so perfect.
我的那段，梅洛拉饰演的简的反应真是太完美了。

451
00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:14.670
I knew I was setting her up for a great reaction.
我知道我是在为她铺垫一个精彩的反应。

452
00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:16.490
And that's always fun to do.
而那样做总是很有趣。

453
00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:20.750
I thought the other brilliant thing about it, Ange, was that you were also setting up
安吉，我觉得这其中另一个高明之处在于，你还构建了

454
00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:22.430
the world beyond the conference room.
会议室之外的世界。

455
00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:26.310
I mean, you knew it was empty out there.
我是说，你知道外面是空的。

456
00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:26.670
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

457
00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:28.070
But you were filling it in.
但你却把它填补了起来。

458
00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:31.250
It was nice to imagine that Michael was in his office.
想象迈克尔在办公室里感觉真好。

459
00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:32.210
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

460
00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:33.130
Thank you.
谢谢。

461
00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:33.650
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

462
00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:37.750
Well, Oscar's going to have a talking head where he said it's probably Michael
奥斯卡会有一个访谈镜头，他说那很可能是迈克尔干的，

463
00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:40.950
because every time money has gone missing, it's been Michael's fault.
因为每次钱不见了，都是迈克尔的错。

464
00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:45.790
I love that he says he goes out with, like, clients for lunch, and then it's a $50 receipt
我喜欢他说迈克尔总是和客户吃午饭，然后拿出一张50美元的收据，

465
00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:46.410
to J.Crew.
还是J.Crew的。

466
00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:50.270
I'm surprised to find out that Michael shops at J.Crew.
我很惊讶迈克尔竟然在J.Crew买东西。

467
00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:51.690
Oh, that is true.
哦，那是真的。

468
00:21:52.150 --> 00:21:55.970
Oscar and Angela both say, you know, listen, we've gone over our books so many times.
