我受不了了。

624
00:28:47.440 --> 00:28:52.100
The only thing I ever ask for for my birthday and for Christmas is a chocolate meringue pie.
我过生日和过圣诞节唯一的要求就是巧克力蛋白派。

625
00:28:52.460 --> 00:28:55.440
My husband makes the best chocolate meringue pie.
我丈夫做的巧克力蛋白派是最好吃的。

626
00:28:55.600 --> 00:28:57.780
Look, I have to curse because it's that good.
听着，我得爆句粗口，因为它实在太好吃了。

627
00:28:58.080 --> 00:29:00.200
And then you have a piece for breakfaSt.
然后你早餐就吃上一块。

628
00:29:00.200 --> 00:29:00.800
I do.
我确实会吃。

629
00:29:00.820 --> 00:29:09.540
Or I just get out the pie pan and stand in the pantry with a fork and eat it out of the pie pan.
或者我干脆拿出派盘，站在储藏室里，拿着叉子直接从派盘里吃。

630
00:29:10.060 --> 00:29:11.480
Sorry, I got a little excited there.
抱歉，我刚才有点激动了。

631
00:29:11.900 --> 00:29:12.860
Where are we?
我们说到哪了？

632
00:29:13.100 --> 00:29:15.220
Well, bottom line is Meredith didn't do it.
总之，梅雷迪思没做那件事。

633
00:29:15.420 --> 00:29:16.740
Meredith did not do it.
梅雷迪思确实没做。

634
00:29:16.860 --> 00:29:19.460
We're on to episode number four called Stanley.
我们进入了第四集，名为《斯坦利》。

635
00:29:20.260 --> 00:29:22.620
Yes, we're back in the conference room.
没错，我们回到了会议室。

636
00:29:22.760 --> 00:29:25.720
The accountants are questioning Stanley regarding the missing money.
会计们正在就丢失的钱盘问斯坦利。

637
00:29:25.880 --> 00:29:27.220
He is delighted by this.
他对此感到很高兴。

638
00:29:27.220 --> 00:29:32.860
Yes, Kevin is going to have our recap talking head where he explains what's going on.
是的，凯文要进行我们的回顾访谈，解释发生了什么。

639
00:29:33.040 --> 00:29:38.720
And then Oscar tells Stanley, listen, I know it's not you, but I have to ask anyway.
然后奥斯卡告诉斯坦利，听着，我知道不是你，但我还是得问。

640
00:29:38.960 --> 00:29:42.500
And Stanley says he hopes whoever did it gets away with it.
斯坦利说他希望做这件事的人能逍遥法外。

641
00:29:42.860 --> 00:29:43.280
I know.
我知道。

642
00:29:44.140 --> 00:29:48.840
Stanley says, in fact, if he finds out who it is, he's going to shake their hand, pat them on the back,
斯坦利说，事实上，如果他发现是谁干的，他会去握住对方的手，拍拍他们的背，

643
00:29:48.940 --> 00:29:52.940
and give them 72 hours to flee the country before telling us who it is.
并给他们72小时逃离这个国家，然后再告诉我们是谁干的。

644
00:29:53.040 --> 00:29:54.000
That made me laugh.
那段把我逗笑了。

645
00:29:54.140 --> 00:29:55.300
I'm like, what?
我当时想，什么？

646
00:29:55.300 --> 00:29:58.480
I love that he has a whole exit strategy for this person.
我喜欢他为这个人制定了一整套撤离计划。

647
00:29:58.920 --> 00:30:03.840
I really noticed the tight angles on this particular scene.
我特别注意到了这一幕中紧凑的拍摄角度。

648
00:30:04.320 --> 00:30:09.080
Randall was working very hard to avoid shooting through the window to the bullpen.
兰德尔非常努力地避免透过窗户拍摄办公区。

649
00:30:09.660 --> 00:30:17.320
When Leslie, as Stanley, gets up to leave, you do see Kate sitting at her desk in the background.
当莱斯利饰演的斯坦利起身离开时，你能看到凯特坐在背景里的办公桌前。

650
00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:22.600
And it's fast because the whole rest of the bullpen is just empty.
而且镜头很快，因为办公区的其余部分都是空的。

651
00:30:23.260 --> 00:30:26.380
As Stanley leaves the room, Kevin says, I don't think it was him.
斯坦利离开房间后，凯文说，我觉得不是他。

652
00:30:26.460 --> 00:30:28.260
And Angela says, really genius?
安吉拉说，真是天才啊？

653
00:30:28.860 --> 00:30:32.860
This leads to a Kevin talking head that I loved, and I think we need to hear it.
这引出了一个我非常喜欢的凯文的单人访谈，我觉得我们得听听。

654
00:30:33.320 --> 00:30:39.760
Angela thinks it's an insult when she calls me a genius, all sarcastic and whatnot.
安吉拉讽刺我叫我天才时，觉得这是在侮辱我，诸如此类的。

655
00:30:39.760 --> 00:30:41.620
But technically, guess what?
但从技术上讲，你猜怎么着？

656
00:30:41.860 --> 00:30:43.100
I am a genius.
我就是个天才。

657
00:30:43.700 --> 00:30:48.980
When I was a kid, I took an IQ test, and I scored over 100.
我小时候做过智商测试，得分超过了100。

658
00:30:51.580 --> 00:30:54.220
So joke is on you, Angela.
所以安吉拉，你被耍了。

659
00:30:56.940 --> 00:31:00.100
We're finding out all these things about the background characters on this show,
我们正在挖掘这部剧中所有配角的背景故事，

660
00:31:00.140 --> 00:31:02.140
and that's one of the things I love about the webisodes.
这也是我喜欢这些网络短剧的原因之一。

661
00:31:02.360 --> 00:31:02.780
Yes.
没错。

662
00:31:03.160 --> 00:31:04.020
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

663
00:31:04.020 --> 00:31:08.500
But when we were texting with Brian, he shared with us a story about shooting this talking head.
当我们和布莱恩发短信时，他跟我们分享了一个拍摄这个单人访谈的故事。

664
00:31:08.680 --> 00:31:10.100
It's really fun.
真的很有趣。

665
00:31:10.100 --> 00:31:11.120
I want you to hear it.
我想让你听听。

666
00:31:12.200 --> 00:31:17.560
So here's my favorite story from the Accountants webisode series.
这是我最喜欢的《会计师》网络短剧系列里的故事。

667
00:31:17.860 --> 00:31:26.500
By the way, Angela, Jenna, audience listening, I just arrived, no joke, back into Scranton, Pennsylvania.
顺便说一下，安吉拉、珍娜，还有听众朋友们，我刚到，没开玩笑，我回到了宾夕法尼亚州的斯克兰顿。

668
00:31:26.520 --> 00:31:29.500
I am at the Rad, the Radisson Hotel.
我现在就在雷迪森酒店。

669
00:31:29.880 --> 00:31:31.180
I've arrived here.
我已经到了。

670
00:31:31.360 --> 00:31:33.440
I'm very, very excited to be back.
能回来我非常非常兴奋。

671
00:31:33.440 --> 00:31:37.360
And now to be talking to you guys about the Accountants.
现在能和你们聊聊《会计师》这部剧。

672
00:31:37.500 --> 00:31:38.400
Here's my story.
这是我的故事。

673
00:31:38.680 --> 00:31:39.680
We're filming.
我们当时正在拍摄。

674
00:31:40.040 --> 00:31:41.760
No one else is on set.
片场没有其他人。

675
00:31:41.760 --> 00:31:47.140
Me, you, Angela, and Oscar, we are recording.
只有你、我、安吉拉和奥斯卡，我们在录制。

676
00:31:47.280 --> 00:31:50.240
And I'm recording a talking head, a direct address to the camera.
我正在录一个单人访谈，直接对着镜头说话。

677
00:31:50.460 --> 00:31:52.280
And we're in the annex.
我们在附楼里。

678
00:31:53.240 --> 00:31:59.500
My back was to the room with the snacks and by Toby's desk.
我背对着放零食的房间和托比的办公桌。

679
00:31:59.980 --> 00:32:02.760
And I'm recording a talking head, and I'm talking to the camera.
我正在录单人访谈，对着镜头说话。

680
00:32:02.760 --> 00:32:08.480
And just behind the camera, I see, as we're recording, Greg Daniels walked by.
就在录制的时候，我看到格雷格·丹尼尔斯从摄像机后面走过。

681
00:32:08.900 --> 00:32:15.920
And I see my old friend from high school, Ed Helms, walked by the camera.
我还看到我高中时的老朋友艾德·赫尔姆斯从摄像机旁走过。

682
00:32:16.060 --> 00:32:24.760
Now, in that moment, I'm not thinking, oh, there's Ed Helms, star of The Daily Show, comedian and actor.
在那一刻，我没想什么“噢，那是艾德·赫尔姆斯，《每日秀》的明星，喜剧演员兼演员”。

683
00:32:24.760 --> 00:32:26.920
My brain didn't go there.
我的大脑没往那方面想。

684
00:32:27.100 --> 00:32:30.400
My brain went back to high school in Atlanta, Georgia.
我的大脑回到了佐治亚州亚特兰大的高中时代。

685
00:32:30.600 --> 00:32:32.620
I was like, Ed Helms?
我当时心想，艾德·赫尔姆斯？

686
00:32:32.860 --> 00:32:38.500
Why is my old buddy Ed Helms on The Office set?
为什么我的老伙计艾德·赫尔姆斯会在《办公室》的片场？

687
00:32:38.500 --> 00:32:42.120
But come to find out, he was there meeting with Greg.
后来才知道，他是去见格雷格的。

688
00:32:42.440 --> 00:32:48.780
He had a deal with NBC, and he was meeting with Greg about joining The Office in season three.
他和NBC有合约，他去见格雷格是为了商谈加入《办公室》第三季的事。

689
00:32:49.600 --> 00:32:53.060
This was his, like, introductory meeting with Greg Daniels.
这算是他与格雷格·丹尼尔斯的初次会面。

690
00:32:53.060 --> 00:32:59.480
So I saw him, gave him a hug, and remember saying so specifically, why are you here?
所以我看到了他，给了他一个拥抱，还记得当时特别问了一句：你为什么在这儿？

691
00:32:59.620 --> 00:33:03.120
Which, in retrospect, it was very embarrassing.
回想起来，这真是太尴尬了。

692
00:33:05.300 --> 00:33:06.780
That is so crazy.
那真是太疯狂了。

693
00:33:07.040 --> 00:33:08.280
Isn't that so wild?
是不是很离谱？

694
00:33:08.340 --> 00:33:09.900
And I totally hear that.
我完全能理解那种感觉。

695
00:33:09.900 --> 00:33:12.460
You know when you see someone completely out of contact?
你知道那种在完全不相关的场合看到某人的感觉吗？

696
00:33:12.520 --> 00:33:12.880
Yes.
知道。

697
00:33:12.880 --> 00:33:14.540
And you can't connect the dots?
就是那种大脑短路的感觉？

698
00:33:14.720 --> 00:33:14.960
Yes.
是的。

699
00:33:15.340 --> 00:33:20.060
I just thought that was so wild to see your old high school friend all of a sudden at your place of work.
我只是觉得突然在工作场所看到高中老友，这太离谱了。

700
00:33:20.160 --> 00:33:20.540
You're like, what?
你会想，什么情况？

701
00:33:20.640 --> 00:33:21.140
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

702
00:33:21.520 --> 00:33:27.800
Well, we also got several fan questions about Kevin's talking head, where he's talking about his IQ score.
嗯，我们还收到了一些粉丝关于凯文访谈片段的提问，他在那段里提到了自己的智商分数。

703
00:33:28.060 --> 00:33:29.960
One is from Amelia S.
其中一个来自俄亥俄州阿克伦市的阿米莉亚·S。

704
00:33:30.040 --> 00:33:35.960
in Akron, Ohio, who said, please do a breakdown deep dive on IQs or IQ tests.
她说，请深入剖析一下智商或智商测试。

705
00:33:36.340 --> 00:33:42.240
And Ivy from Canada said, Kevin says he scored over 100 on an IQ teSt.
还有来自加拿大的艾薇说，凯文称他在智商测试中得分超过100。

706
00:33:42.240 --> 00:33:48.640
The average IQ in the world in the 1970s, estimating when he may have taken it, was 90.
20世纪70年代，也就是推测他可能参加测试的那个年代，全球平均智商是90。

707
00:33:49.380 --> 00:33:51.640
Average IQ has dropped over the years.
平均智商这些年来一直在下降。

708
00:33:51.640 --> 00:33:54.200
It was 87 in 2024.
2024年时是87。

709
00:33:54.340 --> 00:33:59.500
But nonetheless, does this mean that Kevin had an above average IQ as a child?
但尽管如此，这是否意味着凯文小时候的智商高于平均水平？

710
00:34:00.100 --> 00:34:02.820
Well, you know I've never been so excited to deep dive something.
嗯，你知道我从来没对深入研究什么东西这么兴奋过。

711
00:34:02.820 --> 00:34:07.540
I was going to say, I mean, this call to action from Amelia, you must have been like, hey.
我正想说，我是指，阿米莉亚发出的这个号召，你当时一定觉得，嘿。

712
00:34:08.260 --> 00:34:09.500
I was very excited.
我非常兴奋。

713
00:34:09.500 --> 00:34:14.380
I was also very intrigued when Ivy said that IQ scores had been dropping.
当艾薇说智商分数一直在下降时，我也非常好奇。

714
00:34:14.660 --> 00:34:16.260
I had to know everything.
我必须了解一切。

715
00:34:16.640 --> 00:34:16.720
Oh my, yes.
天哪，没错。

716
00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:18.800
All right, here's what I found out.
好了，这是我查到的结果。

717
00:34:18.900 --> 00:34:23.780
There are so many different IQ tests, and they all have different ways that they score.
智商测试种类繁多，它们的评分方式各不相同。

718
00:34:24.020 --> 00:34:24.520
Okay.
好的。

719
00:34:24.520 --> 00:34:32.880
But in general, almost all of them say that 100 is like their median score.
但总的来说，几乎所有测试都将100分视为中位数分数。

720
00:34:33.360 --> 00:34:33.960
Oh.
噢。

721
00:34:34.140 --> 00:34:42.360
And so in general, a score of 85 to 114 signifies average intelligence.
所以通常情况下，85到114分代表智力处于平均水平。

722
00:34:42.920 --> 00:34:43.180
Okay.
好的。

723
00:34:43.460 --> 00:34:50.860
So what we've learned is that Kevin is of average intelligence, according to his reporting of his IQ score.
所以我们了解到，根据凯文自己报告的智商分数，他的智力处于平均水平。

724
00:34:51.020 --> 00:34:53.100
Although Kevin thinks he's a genius.
尽管凯文认为自己是个天才。

725
00:34:53.100 --> 00:34:54.180
Yes, I guess so.
是的，我想是这样。

726
00:34:54.660 --> 00:35:01.920
If you have an IQ score of 115 to 129, you are above average or bright.
如果你的智商分数在115到129之间，说明你高于平均水平或很聪明。

727
00:35:02.540 --> 00:35:07.660
If your score is 130 to 144, you are moderately gifted.
如果你的分数在130到144之间，说明你属于中等天赋。

728
00:35:08.920 --> 00:35:12.740
145 to 159 is highly gifted.
145到159属于高天赋。

729
00:35:12.740 --> 00:35:17.900
And it is estimated that Einstein's IQ was around 160.
据估计，爱因斯坦的智商在160左右。

730
00:35:18.640 --> 00:35:19.180
Dang.
厉害。

731
00:35:19.640 --> 00:35:23.000
I love that that's my response to someone who's really smart.
我喜欢我这种对聪明人的回应方式。

732
00:35:23.280 --> 00:35:23.920
Like, dang.
就像是，厉害。

733
00:35:24.580 --> 00:35:24.760
Dang.
厉害。

734
00:35:25.220 --> 00:35:25.320
Dang.
厉害。

735
00:35:25.320 --> 00:35:25.760
Shit.
天哪。

736
00:35:25.760 --> 00:35:27.760
That's some impressive stuff.
那真是令人印象深刻。

737
00:35:28.400 --> 00:35:30.040
You go, Einstein.
干得好，爱因斯坦。

738
00:35:30.220 --> 00:35:31.640
Einstein, I'm so proud of you.
爱因斯坦，我真为你感到骄傲。

739
00:35:32.820 --> 00:35:38.760
Well, about 98% of people have a score 130 or below.
嗯，大约98%的人分数在130或以下。

740
00:35:39.120 --> 00:35:43.000
Only 2% of the population score above that.
只有2%的人口得分高于这个数值。

741
00:35:43.160 --> 00:35:48.920
So only 2% of people are considered moderately to highly gifted.
所以只有2%的人被认为具有中等到高等天赋。

742
00:35:49.920 --> 00:36:01.700
According to 2019's The Intelligence of the Nations report, the average IQ in the United States was 97.43.
根据2019年的《国家智力报告》，美国的平均智商为97.43。

743
00:36:02.020 --> 00:36:02.360
Uh-oh.
呃哦。

744
00:36:02.460 --> 00:36:03.220
Where is this leading?
这说明了什么？

745
00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:04.260
Where do we rank?
我们排名如何？

746
00:36:04.260 --> 00:36:06.120
We're doing well globally.
我们在全球范围内表现不错。

747
00:36:06.400 --> 00:36:06.600
Okay.
好的。

748
00:36:06.720 --> 00:36:08.440
There was a 2010 study.
有一项2010年的研究。

749
00:36:08.440 --> 00:36:11.520
It took the scores of 108 nations.
它采集了108个国家的分数。

750
00:36:11.840 --> 00:36:11.980
Okay.
好的。

751
00:36:12.120 --> 00:36:16.740
And found that the average IQ across that global sample was 89.
结果发现，全球样本的平均智商为89。

752
00:36:17.400 --> 00:36:17.620
Okay.
好的。

753
00:36:18.120 --> 00:36:24.200
Now, it's very important to note that these kinds of tests can be misinterpreted.
现在，非常重要的一点是，这类测试可能会被误读。

754
00:36:24.300 --> 00:36:26.300
They can be culturally biased.
它们可能存在文化偏见。

755
00:36:26.960 --> 00:36:32.340
Different countries have different ideas of what intelligence is and how to measure it.
不同国家对智力的定义以及衡量方式各有不同。

756
00:36:32.340 --> 00:36:42.340
But, in fact, IQ testing is sometimes considered controversial because intelligence measurements, they can be misinterpreted.
但事实上，智商测试有时会被认为存在争议，因为智力测量结果可能会被误读。

757
00:36:42.980 --> 00:36:47.320
They can be misused to stigmatize marginalized groups.
它们可能被滥用来给边缘群体贴上负面标签。

758
00:36:48.210 --> 00:36:56.380
Also, most IQ tests do not evaluate other important aspects of human functioning like emotional intelligence.
此外，大多数智商测试并没有评估人类功能中其他重要的方面，比如情商。

759
00:36:56.920 --> 00:36:58.860
No offense to Kevin.
无意冒犯凯文。

760
00:36:59.700 --> 00:37:03.600
Kevin, I'm not sure he's going to score very highly in that category either.
凯文，我不确定他在那一项上能得高分。

761
00:37:03.840 --> 00:37:04.760
I'm thinking not.
我觉得不会。

762
00:37:05.040 --> 00:37:05.360
Okay.
好的。

763
00:37:05.700 --> 00:37:12.380
All of that said, it is true that IQ test scores have been dropping since the turn of the millennium,
话虽如此，智商测试分数自千禧年之交以来确实一直在下降，

764
00:37:12.500 --> 00:37:21.060
and many experts believe that it is because we have upped our reliance on technology that we simply do not use our brains as much.
许多专家认为这是因为我们越来越依赖科技，导致我们不再像以前那样动脑了。

765
00:37:21.740 --> 00:37:23.500
Well, that tracks, I think.
嗯，我觉得这说得通。

766
00:37:23.840 --> 00:37:24.040
Yeah.
是啊。

767
00:37:24.220 --> 00:37:26.420
Like, we all want to find the shortcut, right?
就像我们都想找捷径，对吧？

768
00:37:26.620 --> 00:37:29.000
