00:43:26.280 --> 00:43:29.640
If you go to 14 seconds, you can see how the scene is framed.
如果你看到14秒处，就能看出这个场景是怎么构图的。

944
00:43:29.640 --> 00:43:34.800
And, you know, Randall was brainstorming again, how can we be in a scene where we don't see
而且，你知道，兰德尔当时又在集思广益，我们怎么才能拍一场戏，却看不到

945
00:43:34.800 --> 00:43:35.400
the bullpen?
办公区呢？

946
00:43:35.820 --> 00:43:38.440
And I have to say, this is a new accounting stack.
我得说，这是一个新的会计部布局。

947
00:43:38.680 --> 00:43:39.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

948
00:43:39.320 --> 00:43:40.620
Normally, we're at the copier.
通常我们都在复印机那边。

949
00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:42.620
Stacked in a corner this time.
这次被堆在了一个角落里。

950
00:43:42.780 --> 00:43:42.980
Stacked in a corner.
堆在角落里。

951
00:43:43.480 --> 00:43:43.920
Yeah.
是啊。

952
00:43:44.260 --> 00:43:48.180
You know, Oscar says, I don't think it's someone in the office.
你知道，奥斯卡说，我觉得不是办公室里的人干的。

953
00:43:48.820 --> 00:43:50.800
And Angela says, it has to be.
而安吉拉说，肯定就是。

954
00:43:51.160 --> 00:43:53.280
I have an improv moment here.
我这儿有个即兴表演的片段。

955
00:43:53.440 --> 00:43:53.800
Okay.
好的。

956
00:43:54.440 --> 00:43:58.480
So when we went to do our talking heads, you know, Randall would ask us questions.
当我们去录制采访片段时，兰德尔会问我们问题。

957
00:43:58.480 --> 00:44:03.000
That's what we would always do to kind of get us into the moment, get our character talking.
我们总是这样做，为了让我们进入状态，让角色开口说话。

958
00:44:03.760 --> 00:44:08.460
And the talking head they picked for me was one that I improvised in answer to Randall.
他们选用的那个采访片段，是我即兴回答兰德尔的内容。

959
00:44:08.620 --> 00:44:10.480
It wasn't the scripted one they wrote for me.
那不是他们为我写的剧本台词。

960
00:44:10.520 --> 00:44:13.940
And I thought you could hear a little bit of my Southern accent in it.
我觉得你在里面能听出我的一点南方口音。

961
00:44:14.100 --> 00:44:14.620
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

962
00:44:15.280 --> 00:44:15.520
Yeah.
好。

963
00:44:15.520 --> 00:44:20.420
I do think it's someone in this office, which really breaks my heart to tell you the truth.
我确实认为这是办公室里的人干的，说实话，这真的让我很心碎。

964
00:44:21.480 --> 00:44:23.340
Because I thought we were all good people here.
因为我原以为我们这里都是好人。

965
00:44:24.020 --> 00:44:24.420
Yeah.
是啊。

966
00:44:24.460 --> 00:44:26.740
I heard it when you said, breaks my heart, breaks my heart.
我听出来了，当你说到“让我很心碎”的时候。

967
00:44:26.740 --> 00:44:28.280
Because I thought we're all good people here.
因为我原以为我们这里都是好人。

968
00:44:28.820 --> 00:44:30.180
So that wasn't scripted.
所以那段不是剧本里的。

969
00:44:30.240 --> 00:44:33.180
But I love that we got to play around like that in these talking head moments.
但我很喜欢我们在这些采访片段里能那样自由发挥。

970
00:44:33.840 --> 00:44:37.440
Well, their next strategy is to focus on the warehouse.
嗯，他们的下一个策略是把重点放在仓库上。

971
00:44:38.200 --> 00:44:39.340
Could it be Roy?
会是罗伊吗？

972
00:44:39.600 --> 00:44:41.480
I mean, he's getting married soon.
我是说，他很快就要结婚了。

973
00:44:42.320 --> 00:44:44.580
But Angela does not think Roy would do it.
但安吉拉不认为罗伊会做这种事。

974
00:44:44.680 --> 00:44:46.100
He just has too much character.
他的人品太好了。

975
00:44:46.340 --> 00:44:46.820
That's right.
没错。

976
00:44:47.100 --> 00:44:48.700
And Kevin goes, hold up.
然后凯文说，等等。

977
00:44:49.500 --> 00:44:50.420
Wait a second.
等一下。

978
00:44:50.600 --> 00:44:51.740
You like Roy.
你喜欢罗伊。

979
00:44:52.020 --> 00:44:53.640
And she's like, no, we don't.
她说，不，我们才没有。

980
00:44:54.460 --> 00:44:55.340
That's improbable.
那是不可能的。

981
00:44:55.340 --> 00:44:56.140
I mean, inappropriate.
我是说，那是不恰当的。

982
00:44:56.660 --> 00:45:02.080
We got a fan question from Lydia in Sweden who said, Angela having a crush on Roy.
我们收到一个来自瑞典莉迪亚的粉丝提问，她说，安吉拉暗恋罗伊。

983
00:45:02.340 --> 00:45:08.400
Is this supposed to have happened before or after Roy chose Angela in the episode The Fire?
这是设定在罗伊在《火灾》那一集选了安吉拉之前还是之后？

984
00:45:08.940 --> 00:45:10.180
This was after.
是在那之后。

985
00:45:10.460 --> 00:45:11.840
This would have been after.
这应该是在那之后。

986
00:45:12.120 --> 00:45:12.400
Yes.
是的。

987
00:45:12.960 --> 00:45:13.280
Yeah.
没错。

988
00:45:13.380 --> 00:45:16.020
You know, we've been asked this before during the rewatch.
你知道，我们在重温剧集时以前也被问过这个问题。

989
00:45:16.020 --> 00:45:19.960
And I do think Angela was a little smitten with Roy.
我确实觉得安吉拉当时对罗伊有点动心。

990
00:45:20.400 --> 00:45:20.900
Yeah.
是啊。

991
00:45:20.900 --> 00:45:24.940
And Kevin, being like Angela's idiot brother, is so tickled by this.
而凯文，就像安吉拉那个笨哥哥一样，对此感到非常开心。

992
00:45:25.040 --> 00:45:26.760
He is really going to tease her.
他真的打算好好取笑她一番。

993
00:45:27.140 --> 00:45:27.520
Yes.
是的。

994
00:45:27.740 --> 00:45:33.600
He has a talking head where he's just doing that song, Roy and Angela sitting in a tree.
他有一个采访片段，就在那儿唱那首歌，“罗伊和安吉拉坐在树上”。

995
00:45:33.960 --> 00:45:38.040
But then Angela walks behind him and yells at him to cut it out.
但后来安吉拉从他身后走过，大声叫他住口。

996
00:45:38.220 --> 00:45:39.140
Cut it out, Kevin.
住口，凯文。

997
00:45:39.140 --> 00:45:42.920
I noticed that Stanley was in the background.
我注意到斯坦利当时在背景里。

998
00:45:43.660 --> 00:45:51.140
And we also got a fan question from Tharia D in Spain who said, when Angela is passing
我们还收到一个来自西班牙塔莉亚·D的粉丝提问，她说，当安吉拉从

999
00:45:51.140 --> 00:45:56.380
by the other side of the windows and yells at Kevin to shut up, does this mean that all
窗户另一边经过并大声叫凯文闭嘴时，这是否意味着

1000
00:45:56.380 --> 00:46:01.100
along people have been able to hear talking heads in the office?
一直以来人们都能听到办公室里的采访录音？

1001
00:46:01.580 --> 00:46:05.120
It got me thinking about how many gossips people could have heard.
这让我开始思考，人们到底能听到多少流言蜚语。

1002
00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:07.360
That's a really good question.
这真是个好问题。

1003
00:46:07.620 --> 00:46:10.600
I mean, you have to think in this instance, Kevin is singing.
我的意思是，你得考虑到在这种情况下，凯文正在唱歌。

1004
00:46:10.840 --> 00:46:12.940
So maybe it's like a little louder.
所以声音可能会大一点。

1005
00:46:13.400 --> 00:46:18.440
But my character has a few times where she is in the background of a talking head and she's
但我的角色有几次出现在访谈镜头的背景里，而且她当时

1006
00:46:18.440 --> 00:46:19.180
ticked off.
很生气。

1007
00:46:19.420 --> 00:46:19.600
Yep.
没错。

1008
00:46:19.920 --> 00:46:22.060
They did do that with you a lot, didn't they?
他们确实经常让你这么做，对吧？

1009
00:46:22.180 --> 00:46:22.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1010
00:46:22.980 --> 00:46:26.600
Well, now Roy is in accounting and he's being questioned.
好了，现在罗伊在会计部，他正在接受盘问。

1011
00:46:26.600 --> 00:46:31.080
And I noticed something really creative that Randall did here with his camera work.
我注意到兰德尔在这里的运镜手法非常有创意。

1012
00:46:31.200 --> 00:46:35.700
The scene opens with one of the few wider shots.
场景开始时是一个少见的广角镜头。

1013
00:46:35.700 --> 00:46:42.480
He placed Kate in the foreground at her desk, but he very quickly then punches in.
他把凯特放在前景的办公桌前，但随后很快就推进了镜头。

1014
00:46:42.580 --> 00:46:47.460
But he gives you a sense for one moment of that wider office view.
但他让你在那一瞬间感受到了办公室的全景。

1015
00:46:48.280 --> 00:46:49.920
And Roy's going to say, you know what?
然后罗伊会说，你知道吗？

1016
00:46:50.040 --> 00:46:51.560
I wouldn't do that.
我不会那么做的。

1017
00:46:51.700 --> 00:46:52.500
I don't steal.
我不偷东西。

1018
00:46:52.660 --> 00:46:54.920
And even if I wanted to, I wouldn't know how to.
就算我想偷，我也不知道该怎么偷。

1019
00:46:55.260 --> 00:46:57.220
And Kevin lays it all out for him.
然后凯文把一切都摊开告诉了他。

1020
00:46:57.420 --> 00:46:59.420
Kevin's like, well, you'd have to take it from petty cash.
凯文说，好吧，你得从备用金里拿。

1021
00:46:59.540 --> 00:47:01.100
Roy's like, I don't even know where you keep it.
罗伊说，我甚至不知道你们把钱放在哪儿。

1022
00:47:01.220 --> 00:47:02.480
Kevin says, in Oscar's drawer.
凯文说，在奥斯卡的抽屉里。

1023
00:47:02.940 --> 00:47:04.620
Roy says, well, isn't it locked?
罗伊说，那不是锁着的吗？

1024
00:47:04.760 --> 00:47:06.520
Kevin goes, well, he keeps the key behind the counter.
凯文说，他把钥匙放在柜台后面。

1025
00:47:06.720 --> 00:47:10.360
And Oscar's like, Kevin, why are you telling him how to steal?
然后奥斯卡说，凯文，你为什么要教他怎么偷东西？

1026
00:47:10.880 --> 00:47:12.680
And Roy's like, no, I wouldn't do that.
罗伊说，不，我不会那么做的。

1027
00:47:12.780 --> 00:47:13.260
It's wrong.
那是错的。

1028
00:47:13.400 --> 00:47:14.780
And Angela's like, well, I'm satisfied.
安吉拉说，好吧，我满意了。

1029
00:47:15.020 --> 00:47:15.800
Thank you for your time.
谢谢你的配合。

1030
00:47:16.660 --> 00:47:19.020
And then Kevin says, Roy, one more question.
然后凯文说，罗伊，还有一个问题。

1031
00:47:19.280 --> 00:47:20.440
What do you think of Angela?
你觉得安吉拉怎么样？

1032
00:47:21.180 --> 00:47:22.580
And I have an improv moment.
我当时有一个即兴发挥的时刻。

1033
00:47:22.580 --> 00:47:23.600
What was it?
是什么？

1034
00:47:23.840 --> 00:47:26.520
When Oscar says, you don't have to answer that.
当奥斯卡说，你没必要回答那个问题。

1035
00:47:26.640 --> 00:47:28.940
And Kevin says, but you can if you want to.
然后凯文说，但如果你想回答也可以。

1036
00:47:29.200 --> 00:47:30.080
That was improv?
那是即兴发挥的？

1037
00:47:30.460 --> 00:47:30.720
Yes.
是的。

1038
00:47:31.960 --> 00:47:33.300
I like that a lot.
我很喜欢那个。

1039
00:47:33.760 --> 00:47:34.280
All right.
好的。

1040
00:47:34.440 --> 00:47:37.240
Episode number six is titled The Memo.
第六集标题为《备忘录》。

1041
00:47:37.560 --> 00:47:43.220
At this point, the accountants have ruled out Phyllis, Stanley, Jim, Meredith, and themselves.
此时，会计们已经排除了菲利斯、斯坦利、吉姆、梅雷迪斯以及他们自己。

1042
00:47:44.300 --> 00:47:46.380
Although Angela isn't so sure about that.
虽然安吉拉对排除他们自己这一点不太确定。

1043
00:47:46.920 --> 00:47:49.880
Kevin has a talking head where he says he didn't steal it.
凯文有一个访谈镜头，他说他没有偷。

1044
00:47:49.880 --> 00:47:53.640
And Angela says she is positive it's not Dwight.
而安吉拉说她肯定不是德怀特。

1045
00:47:53.800 --> 00:47:56.460
He has the most integrity of anyone in the office.
他是办公室里最有正直感的人。

1046
00:47:57.200 --> 00:47:57.460
Yes.
没错。

1047
00:47:57.640 --> 00:47:59.020
And then they stare at her oddly.
然后他们奇怪地盯着她看。

1048
00:47:59.300 --> 00:48:03.540
So just a reminder, this was released between season two and season three.
提醒一下，这一集是在第二季和第三季之间发布的。

1049
00:48:03.880 --> 00:48:10.440
So the audience knows that Dwight and Angela are a couple, but the people in the office will not find out until season five.
所以观众知道德怀特和安吉拉是一对，但办公室里的其他人直到第五季才会发现。

1050
00:48:10.840 --> 00:48:11.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1051
00:48:11.600 --> 00:48:14.100
When Phyllis spills the beans in Moroccan Christmas.
当菲利斯在“摩洛哥圣诞节”那一集里说漏嘴的时候。

1052
00:48:14.540 --> 00:48:14.720
Yeah.
没错。

1053
00:48:14.720 --> 00:48:18.520
So I loved that we sprinkled this in to the webisode.
所以我很喜欢我们在网络剧集里穿插的这个细节。

1054
00:48:18.840 --> 00:48:22.580
Well, up next is one of my favorite lines of the accountants webisode series.
好了，接下来是会计系列网络剧里我最喜欢的台词之一。

1055
00:48:22.840 --> 00:48:23.400
What is it?
是什么？

1056
00:48:23.760 --> 00:48:25.880
Angela says to Oscar, did you talk to Kelly?
安吉拉对奥斯卡说，你跟凯利谈过了吗？

1057
00:48:26.180 --> 00:48:27.220
Oscar says, yes.
奥斯卡说，谈过了。

1058
00:48:27.400 --> 00:48:29.020
She told me she didn't do it.
她说不是她干的。

1059
00:48:29.120 --> 00:48:31.840
And then 45 minutes later, the conversation ended.
然后45分钟后，谈话才结束。

1060
00:48:32.080 --> 00:48:32.940
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

1061
00:48:33.560 --> 00:48:39.320
And then Kevin says he talked to Creed and he didn't do it either, although he did offer to sell me some dietary supplements.
接着凯文说他跟克里德谈过了，也不是他干的，虽然他确实提出要卖给我一些膳食补充剂。

1062
00:48:39.920 --> 00:48:45.820
Well, they decide that they're going to write a memo, but first they're going to argue over who gets to write it.
嗯，他们决定要写一份备忘录，但首先他们要争论谁来写。

1063
00:48:46.060 --> 00:48:46.500
That's right.
没错。

1064
00:48:46.640 --> 00:48:47.760
Angela says, I'll write it.
安吉拉说，我来写。

1065
00:48:47.880 --> 00:48:49.700
And then Kevin says, no, I want to write it.
然后凯文说，不，我想写。

1066
00:48:50.040 --> 00:48:53.160
And Kevin's like, come on, you never let me write accounting memos.
凯文就像是说，拜托，你从来不让我写会计备忘录。

1067
00:48:53.320 --> 00:48:55.620
And Angela says, fine, but I'll supervise.
安吉拉说，好吧，但我来监督。

1068
00:48:56.100 --> 00:49:01.820
I want to point out that Kate, Leslie, and Phyllis are all in the background of this.
我想指出的是，凯特、莱斯利和菲利斯都在这一幕的背景里。

1069
00:49:02.280 --> 00:49:08.540
This is the most filled out this rest of this bullpen world has been in any of the webisode.
这是所有网络剧集中，办公区背景人最多的一次。

1070
00:49:08.540 --> 00:49:14.120
So I don't know what happened with everyone's schedule, but everyone was there at the same time for this scene.
我不知道大家的档期是怎么安排的，但这一幕大家都在场。

1071
00:49:14.340 --> 00:49:14.720
For this one moment.
就为了这一刻。

1072
00:49:14.960 --> 00:49:16.300
And Randall took advantage of it.
而兰德尔利用了这个机会。

1073
00:49:16.540 --> 00:49:18.000
Well, I have an improv moment.
嗯，我有一个即兴发挥的时刻。

1074
00:49:18.220 --> 00:49:25.920
As we're leaving the conference room, I improvised shutting the door behind me, knowing that Kevin is right behind me and he'd almost walk into it.
当我们离开会议室时，我即兴表演了随手关门，因为我知道凯文就在我身后，他差点就撞上了。

1075
00:49:26.140 --> 00:49:35.220
I got so tickled rewatching this because if you go to that moment, you can hear Brian as Kevin say, God, because he is so annoyed.
重看这一段时我被逗乐了，因为如果你仔细看那一刻，你能听到布莱恩饰演的凯文说“天哪”，因为他真的很恼火。

1076
00:49:35.220 --> 00:49:40.280
And it makes me laugh every time because Brian and I would do stuff like this to each other.
每次看到这儿我都会笑，因为布莱恩和我经常会这样捉弄对方。

1077
00:49:40.520 --> 00:49:40.800
You would.
你们确实会。

1078
00:49:41.020 --> 00:49:44.740
When we were in scenes together, we like to like mess around with each other.
当我们一起拍戏时，我们喜欢互相搞怪。

1079
00:49:44.820 --> 00:49:47.600
And he's really like the brother I never had.
他真的就像我从未有过的亲兄弟一样。

1080
00:49:47.780 --> 00:49:49.500
And this was me just messing with him.
这纯粹是我在捉弄他。

1081
00:49:49.920 --> 00:49:54.040
Well, now Kevin is typing the memo, but Angela is micromanaging him.
好了，现在凯文在打备忘录，但安吉拉在对他进行微观管理。

1082
00:49:54.180 --> 00:49:54.520
Yes.
是的。

1083
00:49:54.700 --> 00:49:55.340
Over his shoulder.
就在他肩膀后面盯着。

1084
00:49:55.520 --> 00:49:59.780
He clearly does not know what it means to make the date right justified.
他显然不知道怎么把日期右对齐。

1085
00:50:00.260 --> 00:50:00.480
Nope.
没错。

1086
00:50:00.960 --> 00:50:04.360
I mean, this is what we were just talking about before.
我的意思是，这就是我们刚才讨论的。

1087
00:50:04.860 --> 00:50:08.220
Now, like our computers write our memos for us.
现在，就像我们的电脑替我们写备忘录一样。

1088
00:50:08.340 --> 00:50:11.640
We don't have to learn proper memo or letter writing.
我们不需要学习如何正确地写备忘录或信件了。

1089
00:50:11.940 --> 00:50:12.860
Oh, yeah, for sure.
哦，确实，肯定的。

1090
00:50:12.960 --> 00:50:13.600
There's templates.
现在都有模板了。

1091
00:50:13.860 --> 00:50:15.900
Like if you want to write a resume, there's a template.
