00:56:13.760 --> 00:56:16.160
I assume it was not Steve Carell.
我猜那肯定不是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

1259
00:56:16.540 --> 00:56:20.460
Well, everyone, it was a photo double played by Paul Bunnell.
嗯，各位，那是保罗·邦内尔担任的替身演员。

1260
00:56:21.140 --> 00:56:25.320
And Angela, of course, you knew it wasn't Steve Carell because you were there.
安吉拉，当然，你知道那不是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔，因为你当时就在现场。

1261
00:56:25.500 --> 00:56:25.980
That's right.
没错。

1262
00:56:26.180 --> 00:56:28.420
I love that it sold that moment, though.
但我很喜欢那个镜头，它成功营造了那种氛围。

1263
00:56:28.640 --> 00:56:29.900
It really helped.
真的很有帮助。

1264
00:56:30.060 --> 00:56:36.740
Although Becky did say, I thought it was weird that Michael didn't have a big goodbye when
虽然Becky确实说，我觉得迈克尔离开办公室时没有一场盛大的告别仪式很奇怪。

1265
00:56:36.740 --> 00:56:37.820
he leaves the office.
他离开办公室。

1266
00:56:37.820 --> 00:56:45.120
Because the top of this next webisode is going to begin with Michael leaving.
因为下一集网络剧的开头就是迈克尔离开。

1267
00:56:45.920 --> 00:56:51.000
And this makes it possible for the accountants to go into his office and start poking around.
这让会计们有机会进入他的办公室开始四处打探。

1268
00:56:51.700 --> 00:56:55.700
But before they go into Michael's office, they're kind of on a stakeout.
但在他们进入迈克尔的办公室之前，他们就像是在蹲点一样。

1269
00:56:55.920 --> 00:56:57.400
They're just waiting for Michael to leave.
他们只是在等迈克尔离开。

1270
00:56:57.980 --> 00:56:59.520
Kevin says, what time is it?
凯文问，现在几点了？

1271
00:56:59.600 --> 00:57:00.560
Like, why hasn't he gone?
就像是，他为什么还没走？

1272
00:57:00.680 --> 00:57:01.520
What time is it?
现在几点了？

1273
00:57:01.680 --> 00:57:05.360
And Angela says, why don't you check the clock for yourself?
安吉拉说，你为什么不自己看时钟呢？

1274
00:57:05.360 --> 00:57:08.280
And he's like, why don't you just tell me what time it is?
他说，你为什么不能直接告诉我几点了？

1275
00:57:08.360 --> 00:57:10.500
And she's like, I think people should be self-sufficient.
她说，我觉得人应该学会自力更生。

1276
00:57:10.980 --> 00:57:12.480
Well, Kevin thinks she's mean.
嗯，凯文觉得她很刻薄。

1277
00:57:13.240 --> 00:57:15.220
This really ruffles her feathers.
这真的让她很不爽。

1278
00:57:15.360 --> 00:57:17.940
In the script, it says Angela makes busy work.
剧本里写着安吉拉在忙活手头的工作。

1279
00:57:18.620 --> 00:57:21.600
And then Kevin and Oscar sort of have this conversation.
然后凯文和奥斯卡进行了这样的对话。

1280
00:57:21.860 --> 00:57:24.960
Oscar's going to the mall because he needs a new walk.
奥斯卡要去商场，因为他需要换个走路姿势。

1281
00:57:25.120 --> 00:57:28.060
And then Angela just blurts out, you know, I'm not mean.
然后安吉拉突然脱口而出，你知道吗，我并不刻薄。

1282
00:57:28.060 --> 00:57:36.760
Oh, lady, I have an audio clip because for whatever reason, Angela is going to apologize.
噢，天哪，我有一段音频，因为不管出于什么原因，安吉拉要道歉了。

1283
00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:42.560
She's going to say sorry twice, not once, but twice.
她要说两次对不起，不是一次，而是两次。

1284
00:57:42.580 --> 00:57:47.840
And I thought we had to hear it because I'm fairly certain these are the only times the words
我觉得我们必须听听，因为我相当确定这是安吉拉·马丁这辈子唯一说过

1285
00:57:47.840 --> 00:57:50.920
I'm sorry come out of Angela Martin's mouth ever.
“对不起”这几个字的时候。

1286
00:57:51.640 --> 00:57:53.580
I'm sorry if I was mean.
如果我刚才刻薄了，我很抱歉。

1287
00:57:57.530 --> 00:57:58.210
It's okay.
没关系。

1288
00:57:59.070 --> 00:57:59.810
Thank you.
谢谢。

1289
00:58:04.420 --> 00:58:06.360
That was uncomfortable.
那真是太尴尬了。

1290
00:58:11.150 --> 00:58:11.990
Okay, let's go.
好了，我们走吧。

1291
00:58:12.170 --> 00:58:13.310
This is so much fun.
这太有趣了。

1292
00:58:13.530 --> 00:58:14.830
It's not supposed to be fun.
这可不是为了好玩。

1293
00:58:16.530 --> 00:58:18.030
Again, sorry.
再说一次，对不起。

1294
00:58:19.550 --> 00:58:20.510
Two sorries.
两次道歉。

1295
00:58:20.730 --> 00:58:21.350
I know.
我知道。

1296
00:58:22.030 --> 00:58:22.510
Wow.
哇。

1297
00:58:22.710 --> 00:58:23.170
I know.
我知道。

1298
00:58:23.370 --> 00:58:27.270
I guess she clearly cares about Kevin thinking if she's mean or not.
看来她确实很在意凯文是否觉得她刻薄。

1299
00:58:27.370 --> 00:58:28.810
In the webisodes, she does.
在网络剧里，她是这样的。

1300
00:58:28.930 --> 00:58:30.070
At least in this world.
至少在这个世界里是这样。

1301
00:58:30.610 --> 00:58:32.770
But it's not going to stop her from being mean.
但这并不能阻止她继续刻薄。

1302
00:58:32.770 --> 00:58:40.650
Well, as they walk over to Michael's office, Kevin does this very funny sort of dance move
嗯，当他们走向迈克尔的办公室时，凯文做了一个非常滑稽的舞蹈动作

1303
00:58:40.650 --> 00:58:42.190
towards Michael's office.
朝迈克尔的办公室走去。

1304
00:58:42.430 --> 00:58:48.130
In the script, it says, Kevin does the Jim Belushi slash Animal House entering the dean's
剧本里写的是，凯文模仿吉姆·贝鲁西在《动物屋》里进入院长

1305
00:58:48.130 --> 00:58:49.390
office stealth maneuver.
办公室时的潜行姿势。

1306
00:58:49.390 --> 00:58:51.990
Yes, it was lost on me.
是的，我没看出来。

1307
00:58:52.110 --> 00:58:54.450
It's also lost on Angela and Oscar.
安吉拉和奥斯卡也没看出来。

1308
00:58:54.970 --> 00:58:55.270
Yes.
没错。

1309
00:58:55.390 --> 00:58:58.310
In the script, it didn't give any stage direction for our reaction.
剧本里对我们的反应没有任何舞台指示。

1310
00:58:58.310 --> 00:59:01.170
But Oscar and I both just chose to be not impressed.
但我和奥斯卡都选择表现得不为所动。

1311
00:59:01.610 --> 00:59:03.430
And Brian improvised.
而且布莱恩即兴发挥了。

1312
00:59:03.590 --> 00:59:05.230
You guys are breaking my spirit.
你们这些人真是让我泄气。

1313
00:59:07.230 --> 00:59:10.490
All right, episode number nine, titled Michael's office.
好了，第九集，标题是《迈克尔的办公室》。

1314
00:59:10.810 --> 00:59:11.630
They are in there.
他们在那里面。

1315
00:59:11.870 --> 00:59:13.890
They are looking through his stuff.
他们在翻他的东西。

1316
00:59:14.230 --> 00:59:15.510
This is my favorite one.
这是我最喜欢的一集。

1317
00:59:15.690 --> 00:59:16.750
This is your favorite?
这是你最喜欢的？

1318
00:59:16.750 --> 00:59:21.410
Yes, because we just were sort of just doing all of these silly bits.
是的，因为我们当时就在做各种傻乎乎的表演。

1319
00:59:21.710 --> 00:59:26.450
And, you know, Kevin has the first line in the webisode, but it wasn't scripted for him
而且，你知道，凯文是网络剧里第一个开口的人，但剧本里没写让他

1320
00:59:26.450 --> 00:59:28.710
to say it into Michael's toy megaphone.
对着迈克尔的玩具扩音器说话。

1321
00:59:28.810 --> 00:59:30.010
I thought that was so funny.
我觉得那太搞笑了。

1322
00:59:30.170 --> 00:59:31.310
Brian just did that.
那是布莱恩自己加的。

1323
00:59:31.310 --> 00:59:32.370
I loved it.
我喜欢这个设计。

1324
00:59:32.510 --> 00:59:34.150
He also added the attention.
他还加了一句“注意了”。

1325
00:59:34.150 --> 00:59:34.550
Yes.
是的。

1326
00:59:35.530 --> 00:59:39.670
Now, the part where he picks up the train whistle and blows it, that was scripted?
那么，他拿起火车汽笛吹响的那部分，是剧本里写的吗？

1327
00:59:39.670 --> 00:59:40.730
That was, yes.
那是的，没错。

1328
00:59:41.070 --> 00:59:46.130
I love that Oscar points out the Seiko timepiece, like, certificate.
我喜欢奥斯卡指出那个精工时钟证书的细节。

1329
00:59:46.130 --> 00:59:47.630
I just loved that.
我太喜欢那个了。

1330
00:59:47.770 --> 00:59:48.090
Yes.
是的。

1331
00:59:48.390 --> 00:59:50.910
And then something odd happens.
然后发生了一件奇怪的事。

1332
00:59:51.250 --> 00:59:59.370
They unlock a drawer in Michael's office, and they find nine Dunder Mifflin snow globes.
他们打开了迈克尔办公室的一个抽屉，发现了九个邓德·米夫林的雪花球。

1333
00:59:59.830 --> 01:00:02.030
It's so interesting.
这太有意思了。

1334
01:00:02.450 --> 01:00:03.090
Why?
为什么？

1335
01:00:03.090 --> 01:00:04.330
Like, why?
就是说，为什么呢？

1336
01:00:04.650 --> 01:00:05.790
What are those for?
那些是用来干嘛的？

1337
01:00:06.050 --> 01:00:06.850
I don't know.
我不知道。

1338
01:00:07.950 --> 01:00:11.610
And Kevin says if he had a snow globe drawer, he'd keep it locked, too.
凯文说如果他有个雪花球抽屉，他也会锁起来。

1339
01:00:11.870 --> 01:00:12.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1340
01:00:13.030 --> 01:00:15.330
Well, Oscar tells Angela to go online.
嗯，奥斯卡让安吉拉上网。

1341
01:00:15.550 --> 01:00:16.850
Look at Michael's Quicken.
看看迈克尔的财务软件。

1342
01:00:17.470 --> 01:00:20.150
I have a little thing to share about this.
关于这一点，我有个小花絮要分享。

1343
01:00:20.290 --> 01:00:21.870
The scene was actually longer.
这场戏其实更长一些。

1344
01:00:22.070 --> 01:00:22.390
Okay.
好的。

1345
01:00:22.530 --> 01:00:25.690
When Angela logged onto the computer, it started like this.
当安吉拉登录电脑时，开头是这样的。

1346
01:00:26.030 --> 01:00:27.710
Angela says, okay, I'm in.
安吉拉说，好了，我进去了。

1347
01:00:27.970 --> 01:00:28.990
Ugh, gross.
呃，真恶心。

1348
01:00:29.470 --> 01:00:30.670
Oscar and Kevin look.
奥斯卡和凯文看了一眼。

1349
01:00:30.930 --> 01:00:32.170
Kevin says, oh, my God.
凯文说，天哪。

1350
01:00:32.530 --> 01:00:33.930
Oscar says, yikes.
奥斯卡说，哎哟。

1351
01:00:34.190 --> 01:00:37.090
Kevin says, that guy must be like 100 years old.
凯文说，那家伙肯定得有一百岁了。

1352
01:00:37.430 --> 01:00:39.190
Oscar says, what's he holding?
奥斯卡问，他手里拿的是什么？

1353
01:00:39.950 --> 01:00:41.950
Kevin says, I think it's a shovel.
凯文说，我觉得那是把铲子。

1354
01:00:42.590 --> 01:00:45.350
And then Oscar says, okay, okay, go check his Quicken files.
然后奥斯卡说，行吧行吧，去查查他的Quicken财务文件。

1355
01:00:46.010 --> 01:00:49.190
What in the world had come up on the computer?
电脑上到底出现了什么？

1356
01:00:49.350 --> 01:00:50.450
What was he Googling?
他当时在谷歌搜什么？

1357
01:00:50.450 --> 01:00:51.850
I don't know.
我不知道。

1358
01:00:52.690 --> 01:00:57.430
The last eight charges were from Jack's Joke and Magic Shop.
最后八笔扣款都来自杰克的整蛊与魔术店。

1359
01:00:57.630 --> 01:00:58.730
He loves that place.
他超爱那家店。

1360
01:00:59.470 --> 01:01:02.130
Angela's going to go ahead and pay his electric bill real quickly.
安吉拉打算顺手帮他把电费交了。

1361
01:01:02.350 --> 01:01:04.390
This was my favorite thing that I did.
这是我做过最喜欢的一件事。

1362
01:01:04.630 --> 01:01:06.390
It was so fun to me.
我觉得特别有意思。

1363
01:01:06.810 --> 01:01:08.510
And when Kevin's like, what are you doing?
当凯文问，你在干嘛？

1364
01:01:08.570 --> 01:01:09.510
I'm like, I'm paying his electric.
我说，我在帮他交电费。

1365
01:01:09.630 --> 01:01:10.850
It's about to be shut off.
电马上就要被停了。

1366
01:01:11.110 --> 01:01:14.830
Well, all of this snooping leads nowhere.
好吧，所有这些窥探都没什么结果。

1367
01:01:15.290 --> 01:01:16.530
They don't find anything.
他们什么也没发现。

1368
01:01:16.750 --> 01:01:18.730
But Angela does pay some of Michael's bills.
但安吉拉确实帮迈克尔付了一些账单。

1369
01:01:18.970 --> 01:01:19.270
Yes.
是的。

1370
01:01:19.270 --> 01:01:21.750
Well, we've made it now to the last one.
好了，我们现在讲到最后一集了。

1371
01:01:21.910 --> 01:01:24.850
It's episode 10 titled, The Best Day of My Life.
这是第十集，标题是《我生命中最美好的一天》。

1372
01:01:25.410 --> 01:01:27.610
It's going to start with Angela and Dwight.
开头是安吉拉和德怀特。

1373
01:01:27.610 --> 01:01:29.210
They're whispering in the kitchen.
他们在厨房里窃窃私语。

1374
01:01:29.710 --> 01:01:34.170
I really feel like these scenes help the writers see Rain and Ice chemistry.
我真的觉得这些场景有助于编剧观察雷恩和艾斯的化学反应。

1375
01:01:35.150 --> 01:01:35.690
Yes.
没错。

1376
01:01:35.950 --> 01:01:38.070
I wanted to play the clip from the scene.
我想播放一下那个场景的片段。

1377
01:01:38.490 --> 01:01:40.310
Rain improvised a moment at the end.
雷恩在结尾即兴发挥了一个动作。

1378
01:01:40.430 --> 01:01:41.430
Let's see if you can guess.
看看你们能不能猜到。

1379
01:01:42.290 --> 01:01:45.690
You're saying Michael stole money from his own company?
你是说迈克尔偷了自己公司的钱？

1380
01:01:46.130 --> 01:01:48.010
Well, we've asked everyone else.
我们已经问过其他人了。

1381
01:01:48.550 --> 01:01:48.970
No.
没有。

1382
01:01:49.430 --> 01:01:49.870
No.
没有。

1383
01:01:50.150 --> 01:01:50.830
That's insane.
这太疯狂了。

1384
01:01:51.050 --> 01:01:51.990
It has to be somebody else.
肯定是别人干的。

1385
01:01:52.450 --> 01:01:53.250
Like Meredith.
比如梅雷迪斯。

1386
01:01:54.550 --> 01:01:55.430
Her creed.
她的信条。

1387
01:01:56.490 --> 01:01:57.390
No, Meredith.
不，梅雷迪斯。

1388
01:01:57.590 --> 01:01:57.890
Definitely.
绝对是她。

1389
01:01:58.510 --> 01:01:59.290
We asked her.
我们问过她了。

1390
01:01:59.470 --> 01:02:00.650
She said she didn't do it.
她说不是她干的。

1391
01:02:00.890 --> 01:02:03.330
Which is exactly what you'd say if you did do it.
这正是如果你干了这事儿会说的话。

1392
01:02:03.730 --> 01:02:04.470
Oh, man.
天哪。

1393
01:02:04.550 --> 01:02:06.670
I should have been handling this investigation from the beginning.
我早该从一开始就接手这项调查的。

1394
01:02:06.670 --> 01:02:08.650
I believe she didn't do it.
我相信不是她干的。

1395
01:02:09.190 --> 01:02:09.270
I believe she didn't do it.
我相信不是她干的。

1396
01:02:09.270 --> 01:02:09.950
Are you doubting me?
你在怀疑我吗？

1397
01:02:12.270 --> 01:02:12.790
No.
没有。

1398
01:02:15.410 --> 01:02:16.370
And here.
还有这里。

1399
01:02:18.490 --> 01:02:19.550
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1400
01:02:19.890 --> 01:02:21.490
There has to be a better explanation.
肯定有更好的解释。

1401
01:02:21.490 --> 01:02:24.570
How did he afford that new water bet he's always bragging about?
他怎么买得起他老挂在嘴边的那台新净水器？

1402
01:02:24.830 --> 01:02:25.470
He charged it.
他刷卡买的。

1403
01:02:25.910 --> 01:02:26.250
Discover.
发现卡。

1404
01:02:26.530 --> 01:02:27.790
Made a little cash back on the deal.
交易还返了点现。

1405
01:02:27.970 --> 01:02:28.430
Smart.
聪明。

1406
01:02:28.930 --> 01:02:37.470
If you were a general in the army and you accused him without proof, you would be court-martialed in front of a firing squad.
如果你是军队里的将军，在没有证据的情况下指控他，你会被送上军事法庭，然后被行刑队枪决。

1407
01:02:38.310 --> 01:02:39.150
That's not true.
那不是真的。

1408
01:02:39.930 --> 01:02:40.270
Okay.
好吧。

1409
01:02:40.530 --> 01:02:42.670
Watch A Few Good Men and tell me that that's not true.
去看看《好人寥寥》，再告诉我那不是真的。

1410
01:02:43.590 --> 01:02:45.650
I own it on DVD if you want to come by later.
我有DVD，如果你想晚点过来看看的话。

1411
01:02:45.870 --> 01:02:46.990
You can't handle the truth.
你承受不了真相。

1412
01:02:47.170 --> 01:02:47.670
Just kidding.
开个玩笑。

1413
01:02:47.850 --> 01:02:48.450
You can't.
你承受不了。

1414
01:02:49.090 --> 01:02:55.150
I mean, I'm assuming it's the little bit about A Few Good Men.
我是说，我猜你指的是《好人寥寥》里的那句台词。

1415
01:02:55.370 --> 01:02:58.530
It's just the very end when he says, you can't handle the truth.
就是最后他说“你承受不了真相”的时候。

1416
01:02:58.690 --> 01:02:59.030
Just kidding.
开个玩笑。

1417
01:02:59.130 --> 01:02:59.510
Yes, you can.
不，你能承受。

1418
01:03:03.980 --> 01:03:06.060
I love early Dwight and Angela.
我喜欢早期的德怀特和安吉拉。

1419
01:03:06.300 --> 01:03:08.700
It just is so fun to rewatch that.
重温那个片段真的太有意思了。

1420
01:03:09.300 --> 01:03:12.100
Well, now, guess what?
好了，现在，你猜怎么着？

